  "findings": [
    "All twelve exact recipes have supported real click/pass actions, no seeded token, modifier, persistent history, permission, choice or fake trigger state. Initial physical sources are Hand/Deck only; initial floating resources/AP are known fixture balances, not claimed histories of how those balances were gained.",
    "The four Ripple recipes activate the real HandUID4 while only Instant-timing activation is legal. Actual discard is cost, resources/AP unchanged; physical owner2 remains pinned in GY. The activation virtual layer correctly pins Controller2/SourceZoneHand/SourceUID4 and does NOT invent a raw Owner1/2 contract.",
    "Ripple resolves while original token-hit layer remains pending; then real HandUID5 Sigil Instant resolves for exactly3HP above the same hit layer. Subsequent original Action-AA token effect must create ZERO tokens. This is observable dependence on original effective Action attribution rather than whichever Instant/mzID most recently resolved. Earlier approved unmodified four red positive pilots create one token without Ripple, so zero-token result is not a standalone all-token-suppressed oracle.",
    "All original AA costs are paid and source printed power/noGA pinned before hitting; real opponent priority is reached before each upper action. HP outcomes for red sources are independently20-power+3; no ability, Sigil or token effect adds AP or resources.",
    "The three Gold cases cover source RGB4/3/2 damage and actual created Gold activation. Source has no GA; initialAP2 minus one AA leavesAP1 to activate Gold legally after real Close. Cost2resources/AP1 and destroy/cannot leave tokenGY occur before draw. Known DeckUID4 reaches Hand only on activation-layer resolution, then own Gold goagain refunds exactlyoneAP. No virtual ability Owner field is assumed.",
    "The five Earth cases generate tokens from actual source hits before a real own end-turn transition. Known Deck defender is drawn during player1 end-turn refill; player2 becomes turn3 active player withAP1/resources0. CreatedEarth remains under player1 control during player2 turn; support WBredUID5/6 then attacks for4.",
    "ComeToFightBlue is Generic NAA defense3, receives+1 per controlled Earth while defending: one token gives total4, two independent actually-created tokens give total5; WB4 deals0. MuscleMuttYellow is an AA defense2 and receives no bonus, so WB4 deals2 and player1 endsHP18. Multiple sources consume their own paid costs/AP and damage opponent7+7=14, leavingHP6, so no player elimination invalidates the stacking fixture.",
    "Source/UID progression matches real physical-card movement and ordinary ABILITY proxies. No virtual trigger token is treated as the physical created token. Activated-layer Owner omitted deliberately; all physical source/token Owners and Controllers remain checked.",
    "Recorder kind=power/go_again dynamically finds the actual current attackUID and persists its absolute mzID. Earth opponent-turn checks therefore must be reviewed later against p2CombatChain-0, not a hardcoded p1 attack reference; no recorder/source change is required.",
    "Earth recipes use native END_PHASE window only as an internal end-procedure/arsenal checkpoint with supported passes. They play/activate nothing there and make no claim of legal rules priority during End Phase. Ponder begin-end-phase timing remains in the separate unapproved held file.",
    "No prevention/Ward decision or frame is part of these twelve dependency cases. All decision_queue_empty assertions are appropriate for their noninteractive supported sequences, and no invented global history/await-frame-empty state is asserted."
  ],
  "source_protocol_basis": [
    "FaBARCAbilityActions/Activate: actual owner-priority and ability timing; virtual ABILITY Controller set, Owner omitted in constructor. FaBARCPayAbility\u2192FaBHVYPaid discards Ripple source; spec destroy invokes actual MONDestroy for Gold before resolution.",
    "Generated Ripple ResolveAbility calls FaBHVYAdd(player,RIPPLE); FaBHVYToken applies RIPPLE only if passed captured effective Action=true. New hit resolver explicitly passes original controller/action even after Sigil overwrote prior macro context.",
    "Generated Gold ResolveAbility draws one. FaBARCResolveAbility then applies own spec goAgain with live turn-player legality. Generic ability resolution returns to saved ACTION or existing DAMAGE stack/priority correctly.",
    "FaBELEDefense counts controlled ArenaEarth only for Action&&!Attack; all one/two-copy/exclusion printed numbers independently checked. FaBFinishEndTurn draws only current player on turn2 and clears assets, then StartOfTurnPhase initializes next player2AP1 and calls Earth start hook only for new controller2, preserving player1Earth.",
    "All exact source files/schema/compiled callbacks/cache and recorder hashes bound in model evidence; no source edit/generation/save is proposed by this review."
  ],
